# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in. Nothing here is read unless you do.
#
# WHERE THE APP LOOKS FIRST
#
# A mobile app cannot ask a server which server it belongs to, so a build ships
# knowing ONE address — the anchor. It asks that address (/app/resolve) which
# server and database to actually use, and the answer comes from the App Servers
# row in Odoo. An admin can move every device by editing that row: no rebuild, no
# per-device setup.
#
# Leave these UNSET and the app behaves exactly as it always has: the 7-tap
# device setup where someone types a URL and picks a database by hand.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are INLINED INTO THE BUNDLE at build time. They are not in
# git, but they are in the app — changing one needs a new build. That is
# unavoidable for the first address; everything behind it stays changeable from
# Odoo.

# The anchor. In production a DOMAIN, so the machine, database and hosting behind
# it can all change without the app noticing. A LAN address works for testing on
# the same Wi-Fi and is unreachable on mobile data — never ship one.
EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ANCHOR_URL=

# Only needed when the anchor host serves SEVERAL databases with no dbfilter:
# Odoo cannot route a public request without knowing the database and answers 404
# instead. This names the ANCHOR's database, never the target's — the target
# still comes from the Odoo row and stays changeable.
# Leave empty on a host with one database or with dbfilter set.
EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ANCHOR_DB=

# Which App Servers row to ask for. Defaults to 369chats; only set this if you
# are building a differently-keyed app against the same server.
EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_KEY=
